<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Este</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Este family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Este was an Italian princely family, named after the town of Este near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padua">Padua</a>, which ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrara">Ferrara</a> from the 13th century and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> and Reggio from 1288. Its rulers, raised to dukes in the 15th century, made Ferrara a leading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> court, patronising Ariosto and Tasso. After losing Ferrara to the Papal States in 1598 the family ruled Modena until 1859, and a German branch gave rise to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-este.jpg" alt="House of Este" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Este_(1).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
